  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S R Raval - Food Inspector vs State Of Gujarat on 3 May, 2018",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. As against that the submission made by the learned counsel for the respondent is that the food article in question was a packaged food article labelled with the complete name and address of the manufacturer clearly indicating that the burden to show that the first respondent was the purchaser of the food article manufactured by its manufacturer was discharged. It is also contended that in absence of the manufacturer and dealer being arraigned as accused, the first respondent could not have been prosecuted. The learned counsel has placed reliance upon State of Gujarat Vs. Manishbhai Narandas Karia [2007 (1) FAC Pg.96]. 4. Thus the burden under Section 19(2) of the Act as interpreted by this Court in State of Gujarat Vs. Manishbhai Narandas Karia (Supra) stood discharged, in this case as well.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. As against that the submission made by the learned counsel for the respondent is that the food article in question was a packaged food article labelled with the complete name and address of the manufacturer clearly indicating that the burden to show that the first respondent was the purchaser of the food article manufactured by its manufacturer was discharged. It is also contended that in absence of the manufacturer and dealer being arraigned as accused, the first respondent could not have been prosecuted.",
    "respondent_arguments": "The learned counsel has placed reliance upon State of Gujarat Vs. Manishbhai Narandas Karia [2007 (1) FAC Pg.96]. 4.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Thus the burden under Section 19(2) of the Act as interpreted by this Court in State of Gujarat Vs. Manishbhai Narandas Karia (Supra) stood discharged, in this case as well."
  },
